# Build context for the repo root — used by server/Dockerfile (api + worker).
#
# The root context only needs sdk/, server/pyproject.toml, server/app/,
# labelers/ and deploy/modal/. Everything listed here is either huge
# (.venv, node_modules), regenerated inside the image (caches, egg-info),
# secret (.env), or irrelevant to a build (docs, git history).
#
# The web image has its own context (./web) and therefore its own ignore
# file: see web/.dockerignore. Rules here do not apply to it.

# --- VCS, CI and editor state -------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.claude
.idea
.vscode

# --- Python -------------------------------------------------------------
# The image installs everything with pip; a host virtualenv or a stale
# egg-info directory copied in would shadow those installs.
**/.venv
**/venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/build

# --- Node / frontend ----------------------------------------------------
# Host node_modules holds binaries built for the host platform and would
# break an arm64 image built on amd64. The bundle is compiled in the image.
**/node_modules
web/dist
web/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# --- Secrets and runtime data -------------------------------------------
# .env reaches the containers through compose (env_file) at run time — it
# must never be baked into an image layer that gets pushed to a registry.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
data

# --- Docs and demo assets -----------------------------------------------
# Nothing in docs/ is a build input; it is screenshots and the demo GIF for
# the README, and they only grow. Excluded as a directory so a new asset does
# not silently start riding along in every build.
docs

# --- Local notes, not published -----------------------------------------
.local

# --- OS junk ------------------------------------------------------------
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
